      "promptEs": "tío",
      "answerEn": "guy; man (informal, especially in Spain)",
      "noteEn": "Tío literally means “uncle,” but in informal Spanish from Spain it can also refer to a man or guy. With an article, as in un tío, it normally names someone; used directly to a listener, it can instead work like informal “man” or “dude.”",
      "example": { "es": "Un tío preguntó por ti.", "en": "A guy asked about you." },
      "tags": ["word", "Spain", "informal", "person", "A2"]
