      "answerEn": "I took; I picked up",
      "noteEn": "Cogí is the completed past form of coger for the speaker. Coger is ordinary for taking or picking something up in Spain, but it has a vulgar sexual meaning in parts of Latin America, where tomar or agarrar may be preferred.",
      "example": { "es": "Cogí un libro de la mesa.", "en": "I picked up a book from the table." },
